Status / Hints / TODO list for MacOS builds

- Requirements:
  - full Xcode; command line tools are not enough for some packages
    (only required on the (virtual) machine *doing* the actual build)
  - autoconf / automake (only for running ./autogen.sh); e.g. from homebrew
    (only required on the machine *controlling* the build)

- Setup:
  - Optionally create src/mac/vmconfig to build on a distinct (virtual) machine
    See src/mac/vmconfig.example.
  - On the builder, you need a case sensitive filesystem, which is not the default:
    sudo diskutil apfs addVolume disk3 APFSX BuildFS
    (assuming disk3 is the "synthesized" disk as given by `diskutil list`)
    This creates and mounts /Volumes/BuildFS . The important spec is "APFSX".

- Building (in gpg4win repo dir):
  echo "default" > packages/BUILDTYPE              # once
  ./autogen.sh                                     # once, and after touching the build system
  ./build.sh --download --mac

- Running:
  Many things will not work properly until bundled/installed. Currently only an
  installation in /Applications/ is supported.

- Implementation Notes / TODO:
  - MacOS cannot run as a docker guest, so we support building in a VM, instead
  - We should write a setup script for that, and/or archive snapshots
  - For the time being, several places assume fixed absolute paths for install locations.
    This may not be entirely uncommon on MacOS, but prevents a portable
    install, ATM. Affected places:
    - gnupg configure flags: So gnupgconf returns correct paths
      - potential alternative: provide gpgconf.ctl
    - gpgme configure flags: --enable-fixed-path, to allow finding gpg
      - potential alternative: require PATH
    - bundling script sets library locations using abs paths
      - potential alternative: convert to @loader_path references
  - Creating a bundle is handled via a python script. python 3.9 is available
    in MacOS 26.05
  - the bundle still has quite a few unused files. Copy rsync filters from
    AppImage, after all? Paths are not the same, however.
  - gpgapplemail needs codesigning to work. codesigning ids are configured in src/mac/vmconfig
  - gpgapplemail needs to be configured with cmake and built using Xcode. As it
    is the only package with that requirement, this is solved via an ugly hack in
    KDEPKG in macimage.mk.in

- Further TODOs:
  - installer is still very basic
  - provide gpgconf.ctl
  - provide signed version
  - provision for gpd vs vsd-builds (later)
  - bundle identifiers currently hardcoded in src/mac/bundle.py
